ore she drops at the daycare on 1/11/2023, she knew the child does not have any bruises that day. But after the parent picked up the child in the afternoon, parent found the bruises and took a picture. The operation failed to file an incident report and did not share to the parent. During the inspection, the operation was asked of any other incident report aside from the 3 dates provided which the parent also provided the same copies. This standard was found to be deficient.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026618496","violation_type_title":"Incident/Illness Report Form Shared with Parent (26 TAC §746.707)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1320273-i20230117-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3501-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1320273-i20230117","date":"2023-01-17","original_code":"746.3501(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-02-27","finding":"Diaper Changing Steps- Prompt: The finding was based on the photos that was sent by the parent and the statement of the former teacher who also has the same concern when her daughter was in the center, she suffered consistent diaper rashes. She would often pick her child from daycare with an extended soiled diaper. This standard was found to be deficient.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026618497","violation_type_title":"Diaper Changing Steps- Prompt (26 TAC §746.3501(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1320273-i20220928","date":"2022-09-28","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905828714","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905828714","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-09-28","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-13202